# SA2A conformance -- graph-global falsifier (N3 denial rule).
#
# TWO ENGINES. This file's `{ BODY } => false .` rule has a verdict on exactly
# one of them:
#
# (a) Praxis seam -- praxis-graphlaw validate_all/check_denials, vendored at
#     priv/graphlaw/praxis_graphlaw.wasm (v26.7.5, intentionally frozen). Its
#     N3_DENIAL dialect reads ADMITTED iff the denial violation list is empty.
#     This file is consumed verbatim on this seam.
# (b) Deployed engine (graphlaw v26.10.28) -- the bare `{ BODY } => false .`
#     fuse is INERT there (non-discriminating). Root cause: purrdf-n3's
#     first-match-only `fired_fuse` (crates/n3/src/parser.rs:1066-1080 parses
#     `=> false` as an inference fuse; crates/n3/src/reasoner.rs:2587-2616
#     returns the FIRST provable fuse and stops), so the consequent carries no
#     verdict. The live denial path on the deployed engine is the
#     denial-sentinel construction in
#     lib/ash_a2a/semantic/hook_reactor/engine.ex: the rule's consequent is
#     rewritten to the condition-fired sentinel
#     <urn:sa2a:hook:condition-fired/1>, and the sentinel appearing in the
#     engine response's `derived` text is the denial verdict.
#
# Graph-global, not per-node: no SHACL shape or ShEx triple constraint
# expresses "no agent anywhere may be simultaneously admitted and revoked" --
# the falsifier is about the co-occurrence of two independent memberships,
# not about one focus node's properties.
#
# base.ttl asserts no ex:Revoked, so the base graph does not trip this denial
# on either engine; negative/falsifier_positive.ttl trips it on the praxis
# seam.

@prefix ex: <http://example.org/sa2a/> .

{ ?a a ex:Agent . ?a a ex:Revoked } => false .
